# Trivy ignore file — Gulley release image.
#
# The service runs TypeScript via `tsx`, so the image ships the full dev/build/
# install toolchain in node_modules. Every CVE below is in a package that is NOT
# in the runtime dependency graph of the gateway/control-api service (verified
# with `pnpm why --prod`) and whose vulnerable code path is never invoked by the
# running service. The esbuild transpiler binary is excluded separately via the
# scan's --skip-dirs. OS packages and genuine runtime libraries are still scanned
# strictly (fail on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL). The durable fix — a distroless image
# with pre-bundled JS and no toolchain in the runtime — is a tracked follow-up
# (see docs/SUPPLY_CHAIN.md).

# brace-expansion (ReDoS) — dev tooling, not in the prod graph
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
# ip-address (inconsistent parsing) — dev tooling
CVE-2026-69192
# js-yaml (DoS) — via eslint, dev tooling
CVE-2026-84375
# pacote — npm install/fetch tooling
CVE-2026-9496
# picomatch (ReDoS) — dev tooling
CVE-2026-33671
# sigstore — npm provenance tooling
CVE-2026-48815
# tar (gzip-bomb / malformed-archive DoS) — npm install tooling
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566
# vite (dev-server fs.deny bypass) — test tooling
CVE-2026-53571
# vitest (UI-server path traversal / RCE) — test tooling, never run in the image
CVE-2026-47429

# @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger — a runtime dependency, but the vulnerable
# JaegerPropagator.extract() path is unreachable here: OTEL_PROPAGATORS is never
# set to jaeger, the gateway registers only tracecontext+baggage, and inbound
# traceparent is parsed by the gateway's own code. Real fix ships with the
# deferred OpenTelemetry 1.x -> 2.x bump.
CVE-2026-59892
